See qa/KNOWN_FAILURE_MODES.md #62 (findings D3-FP, D6, D7).

WHAT IT DOES, on top of e085cfc:
  1. D6 (already live in production at c9dfab5 / v92, NOT introduced by D3):
     `&& lifecycleMismatchCorrections.length === 0` — stop the PAST gate from overwriting
     Brain OS's OWN truthful lifecycle-mismatch correction with a different, less accurate
     one that additionally claims (falsely) that chat cannot do the action.
  2. D3-FP (introduced by e085cfc): PAST_CLAIM_NEGATED — a truthful NEGATIVE
     ("QA-LIFECYCLE-EMPLOYEE2 was not created.") is not a completion claim.
  3. D3-FP: PAST_CLAIM_ATTRIBUTED_ELSEWHERE — a truthful report about a PRIOR turn
     ("they were just restored in the prior turn") is not a claim about THIS turn.
  4. D7: re-attach disambiguation option LABELS, not only pendingAction.question. The
     system prompt puts the option names in `summary`, and matchDisambiguationOption()
     only resolves a reply that CONTAINS a label — so destroying `summary` and restoring
     only `question` leaves a live pendingAction the user cannot answer.

EVIDENCE THIS CANDIDATE WAS ACTUALLY EXERCISED (not just written):
  applied to a scratch copy of index.ts and run against
  qa/scenarios-runner/past_completion_gate_behavior.mjs — Sections A, B and C all pass
  (they do NOT both pass on either master or e085cfc), and Section D correctly flips to
  "D6 appears FIXED". index.ts was then restored byte-identical
  (sha256 8d76f13d0ef9ff97ec1248f13de06ff2fd028e4ae10685d4fc3fca58c16771a4, CRLF working
  tree), `git status` clean for supabase/.

KNOWN LIMITATIONS OF THIS CANDIDATE — read before shipping:
  * PAST_CLAIM_NEGATED and PAST_CLAIM_ATTRIBUTED_ELSEWHERE are tested against the WHOLE
    summary, so a mixed reply ("The approval was not rejected — it has been approved.")
    would be exempted. Sentence-level evaluation, or per-claim grounding against
    factLines, is the real fix; this is a narrowing, not a solution.
  * It has had NO live HTTP acceptance test. Nobody has yet seen this behave in the real
    Edge Function.
  * It breaks one assertion in
    qa/scenarios-runner/d3_past_completion_gate_not_shortcircuited_by_pending_action.mjs
    ("correction preserves a real pending prompt") purely because that assertion hardcodes
    the variable name `pendingPrompt`; loosen that assertion if this ships.

